  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q34-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "34",
    "prompt": "In the expansion of $\\left(x^2+\\frac{a}{x}\\right)^8$, the ratio of the coefficient of $x^7$ to the coefficient of $x^{10}$ is $6:1$. Find $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3$.\n\nMatch the powers in the general term; the coefficient ratio simplifies to $2a$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}T_k&=\\binom{8}{k}(x^2)^{8-k}\\left(\\frac{a}{x}\\right)^k\\\\T_k&=\\binom{8}{k}a^kx^{16-3k}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x^7$, $16-3k=7$, so $k=3$. For $x^{10}$, $16-3k=10$, so $k=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}[x^7]&=\\binom{8}{3}a^3=56a^3\\\\{}[x^{10}]&=\\binom{8}{2}a^2=28a^2\\\\\\frac{56a^3}{28a^2}&=6\\\\2a&=6\\\\a&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
